[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107829,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Calcifying nested stromal-epithelial tumour (CNSET) of the liver is a rare, low-grade hepatic neoplasm of uncertain lineage characterized by a distinctive nested architecture surrounded by a cellular myofibroblastic stroma and psammomatous calcifications.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107830,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8975/1 Calcifying nested stromal-epithelial tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107831,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F70.5 &amp; XH8X78 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of liver, gallbladder, or bile ducts &amp; Calcifying nested epithelial stromal tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107832,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> nested stromal-epithelial tumour; ossifying stromal-epithelial tumour; desmoplastic nested spindle cell tumour; ossifying malignant mixed epithelial and stromal tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107833,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107834,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CNSET most often arises in the right hepatic lobe (65% of cases) {15613852; 15613851; 19363442}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107835,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CNSET is often discovered incidentally, sometimes in patients with a history of a calcified hepatic nodule. Occasional patients present with abdominal pain, a palpable mass, or nausea. Around 20% of patients present with Cushing syndrome {15613852; 19363442}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107836,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "<p>CNSET is rare, with about 40&nbsp;reported cases. There is a female predominance and a predilection for children and adolescents (80% of cases) {15613852; 15613851; 19363442; 31602372}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-17T11:58:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107837,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most CNSETs are sporadic. Several cases have been associated with Beckwith&ndash;Wiedemann syndrome {23570373; 27965001}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107838,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>CTNNB1</em> deletions have been identified in several cases {22749188}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107839,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CNSET is well circumscribed but unencapsulated, with a multinodular, sharp interface with adjacent liver. Tumours range in size from 20&nbsp;to 300&nbsp;mm (median: 125&nbsp;mm). The cut surface is yellow or white and granular {19363442}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107840,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are composed of ovoid to irregular nests of variably spindled to epithelioid cells, cuffed by a cellular stroma. A focally trabecular architecture is sometimes observed. Occasional nests contain central necrosis. The tumour cells are bland and uniform, with vesicular chromatin, indistinct nucleoli, eosinophilic cytoplasm, and low mitotic activity. The nests often harbour psammomatous calcifications, and sometimes ossification. The stroma may contain a bile ductular proliferation.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, the tumour cells are positive for broad-spectrum keratins and WT1 (usually nuclear but sometimes cytoplasmic or paranuclear dot-like), with aberrant nuclear and cytoplasmic &beta;-catenin staining {15613852; 15613851; 19363442; 22749188}. Expression of CD56, EMA, PR, NSE, and KIT (CD117) is variable. Desmin, chromogranin, synaptophysin, HepPar-1 (CPS1), and polyclonal CEA are negative. The spindle cells in the stroma are positive for SMA.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107841,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T10:44:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
